697554551938301,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":6.9,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.20583245261746358,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":55.5,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.12274170366268233,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.022343389416872972,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":31.1,"_gate_rev_durability":0.00032059222965741263,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":25.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.1246082628048792,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.058250066497173236,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.037344079446388054,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":37.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.0173,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":11.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.222,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":22.2,"pf":[],"description_full":"Radian Group Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides mortgage insurance in the United States. It aggregates, manages, and distributes mortgage credit risk for the benefit of mortgage lending institutions and mortgage credit investors through private mortgage insurance on residential first-lien mortgage loans. The company also offers private mortgage insurance, specialty insurance, and reinsurance lines. It serves mortgage originators, such as mortgage banks, commercial banks, savings institutions, credit unions, and community banks. The company was formerly known as CMAC Investment Corp. and changed its name to Radian Group Inc. in June 1999. Radian Group Inc. was founded in 1977 and is headquartered in Wayne, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael Scott Weinbach | CEO & Director | Age 52","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 900 people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $129K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $50K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Radian Group Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.6B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and +0% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +4.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 8% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $116M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.21\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 13\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 12.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (78% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.222},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 43% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 33% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 47% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Large open-market insider purchases (net $4.2M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","33 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Radian Group (RDN) Earnings And Dividend Keep Value In Focus","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-rdn/radian-group/news/radian-group-rdn-earnings-and-dividend-keep-value-in-focus","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794579420.41,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.866,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Radian Group (NYSE:RDN) Stock Gets Price Target Trim from Keefe, Bruyette & Woods","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/radian-group-nyserdn-stock-gets-price-target-trim-from-keefe-bruyette-woods.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794557211.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.459,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Here's Why Radian (RDN) is a Strong Value Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028605/here-s-why-radian-rdn-is-a-strong-value-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_value_score-3028605","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794490803.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.727,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Radian Group declares $0.255 dividend (NYSE:RDN)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4671076-radian-group-declares-0_255-dividend","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794453411.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.459,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"RDN or AXAHY: Which Is the Better Value Stock Right Now?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/rdn-axahy-better-value-stock-154002486.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794411602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.874,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":